Ginger Baker is known for playing in Cream and Blind Faith, but the world's greatest drummer didn’t hit
his stride until 1972, when he arrived in Nigeria and discovered Fela Kuti's Afrobeat.

3
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
After leaving Nigeria, Ginger returned to his pattern of drug-induced self-destruction, and countless groundbreaking musical
works, eventually settling in South Africa, where the 73-year-old lives with his young bride and 39 polo ponies.

